      "claim": "The narrowest functional diameter of the adult female birth canal (obstetric conjugate) is roughly 110 mm (10–11 cm).",
      "evidence": "Obstetrics textbooks (Cunningham et al., 2014) define the normal obstetric conjugate as ≈10–11 cm.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "The skull’s smallest transverse dimension exceeds the smallest pelvic dimension by about 30 mm.",
      "evidence": "Direct subtraction of the measurements from steps 1 (140 mm) and 2 (110 mm).",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1, 2]
    },
