      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Fully fused adult cranial bone is rigid; compressing a 140 mm skull to <110 mm would require forces far beyond physiological limits and would cause fracture.",
      "evidence": "Cortical bone has a compressive yield stress ≈130 MPa; reducing the skull width by 30 mm would demand stresses >200 MPa, exceeding bone strength and causing catastrophic fracture, whereas fetal skulls can mold because sutures and fontanelles are not yet ossified.",
